    "updated_at": "2023-04-06T00:00:09Z",
    "body": "An alternate approach for changing the spec to match the firefox/safari behavior in the above case: lay out the anonymous box twice.\r\n\r\n1. When laying out the principal box, also layout the anonymous content box.\r\n2. Per usual block flow, use the resulting anonymous content box height to resolve the principals box's height, if automatic.\r\n3. Make the resulting principal box height the available *definite* height for laying out the anonymous content box a second time\r\n4. Keep the requirement that specifies the anonymous content box has `block-size:100%`\r\n5. Maybe make the final height of the anonymous content box indefinite? If necessary for compat.\r\n\r\n(Above assumes horizontal writing mode for simplicity. It needs `s/height/block-size/g`)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
