    "body": "> @dholbert - Firefox doesn't currently wrap its contents in an anonymous block for fieldsets right? (Which is why you have this particular behaviour)?\r\n\r\nWe do wrap the contents in an anonymous *box*, which is usually a block, though if the fieldset has `display:flex` or `display:grid` then it'll be one of those.\r\n\r\n[Here's where we create that box.](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/9e3413f54ed6c9165b5659558091d766d34a731f/layout/base/nsCSSFrameConstructor.cpp#3159)\r\n\r\nThis was added in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1230207 (and extended in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1230672 to support multicol as well)\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if this predated the spec text referenced here or not.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
