    "created_at": "2023-04-06T18:29:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-04-06T18:32:27Z",
    "body": "I think so, yeah. (I believe we have that implicitly happening in the code that I quoted above -- in the C++ object that's used there, we have `ComputedMinBSize` canonically representing the minimum content-box size, with `box-sizing` already having been taken into account.)\r\n\r\nI think this works similarly for `<button>` with `display:flex`, too -- there's an anonymous box to wrap the contents, and we transfer min/max constraints through to that anonymous box, so that it can honor `justify-content`.  Here's an example to demonstrate:\r\nhttps://jsfiddle.net/dholbert/9na2um0f/\r\n\r\n(Buttons do also vertically center by default, but that's not what's happening here; you can confirm by removing or adjusting the `justify-content` decl.)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
