    "created_at": "2023-04-13T19:32:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-04-13T19:32:58Z",
    "body": "So the spec change would be to remove\r\n\r\n> The ['block-size'](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-logical/#propdef-block-size) property is expected to be set to '100%'.\r\n\r\nand add instead\r\n\r\n> The computed value of the 'min-block-size' property is expected to be the computed value of 'min-block-size' of the `fieldset` element, substracting the size of the rendered legend (if any) on the block axis, and if the `fieldset`'s computed value of `box-sizing` is `content-box`, then also substracting the size of borders and paddings on the block axis.\r\n\r\n? (I'm here trying to take into account that the `legend` could have a different writing mode.)\r\n\r\nOr is block-size: 100% needed in some cases?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1507509155/reactions",
